## Genome Wide Association (GWAS) for Klebsiella pneumoniae in New Zealand Sea Lions

## Setting up the environment:
```cd 00_nesi_projects/uoo04227/sealions/GWAS
module load PLINK
module load vcftools
plink2 --version
```
Source files have been deleted so I have to filter individuals from vcf rather than running a new popmap. 
vcftools was used to filter out Ivermectin individuals and keep control group individuals. 
Create and upload a text file with IDs for samples you want kept. 

```vcftools --vcf finalsnps.vcf --keep kp_samples.txt --recode --recode-INFO-all --out kp_vcf
```

GWAS analysis of VCF:
NOTE: phenotype file (kp_phenotypev2) must have 3 columns: IID (individual ID), FID (family ID, fill with zeroes), and kp_phenotype (Binary: 1 = control, 2 = case). 
Phenotype info MUST be in the third column. Use --pheno-name to specify column for phenotype data. 
```plink2 --vcf kp_vcf.recode.vcf --pheno kp_phenotypev2.txt --pheno-name kp_phenotype --line
ar allow-no-covars --out kpgwas
```

Accessing California sea lion reference genome:

```module load datasets
datasets download genome accession GCF_009762305.2 --include gff3,rna,cds,protein,genome,seq-report
```
